ORDINANCE XVIII OF 1961
ORDINANCE XVIII OF 1961
WEST PAKISTAN (BOARD OF INTERMEDIATE AND SECONDARY
EDUCATION, LAHORE) ORDINANCE, 1961
2. Definitions.‑In this Ordinance, unless the context otherwise
requires, the following expressions shall have the meanings hereby respectively
assigned to them, that is to say‑
(a) "Board" means the
Board of Intermediate and Secondary Education, Lahore, as reconstituted under
this Ordinance ;
(b) "Chairman" means
the Chairman of the Board ;
(c) "College" means
an institution within the jurisdiction of the Board and recognized for the
Intermediate Education and includes a college, having Intermediate and Degree
classes and affiliated to the University for the Degree classes ;
(d) "Committee" means a committee constituted under this
Ordinance ;
(e) "Controller of
Examinations" means the Controller of Examinations of the Board ;
(f) "Controlling
Authority" means the Controlling Authority of the Board;
(g) "Government"
means the Government of West Pakistan ;
(h) "Head of an
institution" means the principle of a college or the ; Headmaster or Headmistress of a school ;
(i) "institution" means's College or a school;
(j) "Intermediate
College" means an institution recognized for imparting instruction to
Class XI and Class XII and includes an institution having Intermediate and
Secondary classes ;
(k) "Intermediate
Education" means education pertaining to Class XI and Class XII ;
(1) "prescribed"
means prescribed by Regulations or Rules ;
(m) "Principal" means
the head of a College ;
(n) "recognised" means recognised by the Board ;
(o) "Regulations" and
"Rules" mean respectively the Regulations and Rules made by the Board
under this Ordinance;
(p) "school" means an
institution recognised only for the Secondary Education ;
(g) "Secondary Education"
means education pertaining to Class IX and Class X and such other classes as
may be declared by Government to be classes of Secondary Education ;
(r) "Secretary" means the Secretary of the Board ; and
(s) "University"
means the University of the Punjab.
